Revision history for JS::Minifier

{{$NEXT}}
    - Fork of JS::Minify by Sam Morrison
    - Rename module from JS::Minify to JS::Minifier
    - Rename .pm6 to .rakumod, .t to .rakutest
    - All-new CLI tool bin/jsminify with --drop-console,
    --drop-debugger, --keep-bang-comments, --nocompress,
    --strip-debug, --check, --copyright, --output
    - Translate documentation and tooling from Perl 6 / perl6 to Raku
      / raku
    - Add shebang (#!) preservation
    - Add bang-comment (/*! */) preservation
    - Add template literal (backtick string) support with ${}
      interpolation
    - Add NOCOMPRESS block support (/* BEGIN/END NOCOMPRESS */)
    - Add drop_console option to remove console.* calls
    - Add drop_debugger option to remove debugger; statements
    - Shorten true to !0 and false to !1
    - Remove semicolons before closing braces
    - Strip multi-line string continuations (\\ + newline)
    - Track line and column numbers for better error messages
    - Export js-minify alias for backward compatibility
    - Update META6.json with new maintainer, auth, version 1.0.0,
      source URL
    - Update .travis.yml for Raku ecosystem
    - Add comprehensive test coverage for all new features
    - Fix get() guard missing return and off-by-one (<=) causing
      out-of-bounds reads
    - Fix put-literal line continuation (backslash before newline)
      outputting the backslash before detecting the newline
    - Fix EOF handler sending literal '\n' instead of actual newline;
      preserve-endspace already handles trailing newlines correctly
    - Update tests for corrected trailing newline behavior
    - Add test coverage gaps: bare console with drop_console,
      strip_debug at EOF, copyright+nocompress,
      bang-comments+nocompress, nested template literals, true/false
      in object keys, combo flags
    - Add full CLI test suite (t/03-cli.rakutest) covering stdin,
    --nocompress, --check, --version, --help, -o, file args, -s, -b,
    --drop-debugger
    - Fix is-postfix/is-infix/is-alphanum returning True for empty
      strings ('.contains("")' always returned True)
    - Fix put-literal unterminated string detection (when !$delimiter
      smartmatched against Bool False, never triggering)
    - Fix process-comments misclassifying return/regex as division;
      added is-regex-start helper for keywords that start regex
      literals (return, typeof, throw, delete, void, case, new, in,
      instanceof)